      "math_academy_id": "e-5839",
      "problem": "What is the domain of the function $f(x) = \\dfrac{3}{2-x}+1?$",
      "worked_solution": "A reciprocal function is defined for all values of $x$ except those that make the denominator zero. To find the domain, we must exclude all values of $x$ that make the denominator zero.\n\nSetting the denominator equal to zero and solving, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2-x & =0 \\\\ x & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is  $x \\in (-\\infty,2) \\cup (2 ,\\infty).$",
